      "title": "Tailscale didn't stop the Hugging Face intrusion",
      "url": "https://tailscale.com/blog/hugging-face-intrusion",
      "discuss_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49127306",
      "score": 595,
      "comments": 215,
      "author": "bluehatbrit",
      "published": "2026-07-31T19:03:45Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Mesh VPNs like Tailscale secure network transport, but fail to block unauthorized access via compromised application tokens or stolen credentials.",
        "Relying solely on zero-trust overlay networks exposes AI model hubs to application-layer attacks and compromised developer credentials.",
        "AI teams must enforce fine-grained API token scoping, rapid secret rotation, and strict identity-based access control beyond network perimeters."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "rss",
      "subsource": "github.blog",
      "category": "engineering",
      "title": "Don’t stop early: Case-folding source code at memory speed",
      "url": "https://github.blog/engineering/architecture-optimization/dont-stop-early-case-folding-source-code-at-memory-speed/",
      "discuss_url": "https://github.blog/engineering/architecture-optimization/dont-stop-early-case-folding-source-code-at-memory-speed/",
      "score": null,
      "comments": null,
      "author": "Alexander Neubeck",
      "published": "2026-07-31T16:00:00Z",
      "bullets": [
        "GitHub optimized code search case-folding to process >45 GiB/s on a single CPU core, achieving full memory bandwidth speeds.",
        "The technique replaces conventional branching with branch-free loops and byte-space arithmetic to eliminate expensive conditional jumps.",
        "Processing every byte uniformly without early-exit logic delivers higher throughput by preserving hardware CPU instruction pipelining."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "lobsters",
