      "score": 6,
      "comments": 4,
      "author": "hoistbypetard",
      "published": "2026-07-30T14:36:05Z",
      "bullets": [
        "A critical vulnerability (CVE-2026-66066) in Ruby on Rails Active Storage allows unauthenticated remote attackers to achieve arbitrary code execution.",
        "The KindaRails2Shell flaw exploits file transformation pipelines in Active Storage, echoing classic Rails execution vectors through untrusted input parsing.",
        "Development and security teams must audit Rails services, update core dependencies, and temporarily disable Active Storage transformations if unpatched."
      ]
    },
